        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "e75ba723-9c4c-5f93-b622-b52eba702078",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nicholas Barnewall, James II and VII, Patrick Barnewall\n- Titles and Families: Viscount Barnewall, Barnewall family, Lord Trimlestown\n- Places and Institutions: County Dublin, Irish House of Commons\n\nFacts:\n- James II and VII was born on 14 October 1633 and later became King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII.\n- The title Viscount Barnewall was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall.\n- Before receiving the title Viscount Barnewall, Nicholas Barnewall had represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\n- James II and VII reigned from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\n- The third Viscount Barnewall was a supporter of James II and was outlawed.\n- Patrick Barnewall belonged to a junior branch of the Lord Trimlestown family.\n- Patrick Barnewall's own descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.\n- James II and VII died on 16 September 1701.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "835e8e56-d984-500e-9833-af676da9e5c1",
        "text": "Page: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: It was created on 29 June 1646 for Nicholas Barnewall, who had earlier represented County Dublin in the Irish House of Commons.\nPage: Viscount Barnewall. Sentence: His grandson, the third Viscount, was a supporter of James II and outlawed.\nPage: James II of England. Sentence: James II and VII (14 October 1633 – 16 September 1701) was King of England and Ireland as James II and King of Scotland as James VII, from 6 February 1685 until he was deposed in the Glorious Revolution of 1688.\nPage: Patrick Barnewall (Solicitor General). Sentence: He belonged to a junior branch of the family of Lord Trimlestown: his own descendants held the title Viscount Barnewall of Kingsland.",
